881 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "909a9619-c6b0-5d02-8b81-b7f5f009f565" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274924 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186273365 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274924 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186273600 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274924 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186273700 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274924 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186274345 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274924 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186274564 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274924 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274924 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274924 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186273365 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274924 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "a56c7314-1e3c-587a-ae5f-7840c37f76ba" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275207 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186274924 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275207 #edb/ref 1069 "q-149564" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275207 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275207 #edb/ref 1071 "| **Number of Members ($x$)** | $3$ | $4$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Number of Cars ($y$)** | $2$ | $2$ | $2$ | $6$ |\n\nIn a survey of $4$ families, the number of members in each family was recorded as well as the number of cars owned by that family. The data is shown in the table above.\nCompute the covariance of the data sets given that the means are $\\overset{―}{x}=4$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275207 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "478c2f5a-fb6f-5ae6-b9eb-deeec3c02c64" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275207 #edb/ref 1074 "The (population) covariance of the data sets $x={{x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}}$ and $y={{y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n}}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}(x,y)=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}$ are the means of the data sets.\n\nTherefore, the covariance of our data sets is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(3-4)(2-3)+(4-4)(2-3)+(4-4)(2-3)+(5-4)(6-3)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(-1)(-1)+(0)(-1)+(0)(-1)+(1)(3)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[1+0+0+3] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275208 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186274881 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275208 #edb/ref 1069 "q-149570" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275208 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275208 #edb/ref 1071 "| **Years in the 1st division ($x$)** | $44$ | $38$ | $32$ | $30$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Number of Championships ($y$)** | $4$ | $3$ | $3$ | $6$ |\n\nThe table above shows the number of years four English soccer teams have been in the top division and the number of national championships they have won. \nCompute the covariance of the data sets." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275208 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d4368ff5-6ce7-5044-aed6-ebdab8009258" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275208 #edb/ref 1074 "The (population) covariance of the data sets $x=\\{{x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}\\}$ and $y=\\{{y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n}\\}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}(x,y)=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}$ are the means of the data sets.\n\nFirst, we need to compute the means:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (44+38+32+30) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 144 \\\\  & =36 \\\\ \\overset{―}{y} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (4+3+3+6) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 16 \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the covariance of our data sets is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(44\\,-\\,36)(4\\,-\\,4)+(38\\,-\\,36)(3\\,-\\,4)+(32\\,-\\,36)(3\\,-\\,4)+(30\\,-\\,36)(6\\,-\\,4)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(8)(0)+(2)(-1)+(-4)(-1)+(-6)(2)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[0+(-2)+4+(-12)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (-10) \\\\  & =-2.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275214 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186274870 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275214 #edb/ref 1069 "q-149617" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275214 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275214 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following data sets:\n\n$$\nx=\\{6,\\,4,\\,8,\\,6\\},\\,y=\\{4,\\,7,\\,11,\\,14\\}\n$$\n\nYou're given that $\\overset{―}{x}=6$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=9.$ Calculate $\\text{Cov}(x,y).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275214 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f9c47870-1c3c-5cbd-a10d-e30d2edb18f8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275214 #edb/ref 1074 "The (population) covariance of the data sets $x=\\{{x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}\\}$ and $y=\\{{y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n}\\}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}(x,y)=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}$ are the means of the data sets.\n\nTherefore, the covariance of our data sets is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(6-6)(4-9)+(4-6)(7-9)+(8-6)(11-9)+(6-6)(14-9)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(0)(-5)+(-2)(-2)+(2)(2)+(0)(5)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[0+4+4+0] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
